<PageLayout title="Starter Log" subtitle="A printable template for tracking your starter itself, over time.">

  <p>A baking log tracks one bake. This one tracks the culture behind every bake — the thing that has to stay healthy for any of the rest of this to work. Use it to keep an eye on feeding ratio, time-to-peak, how often you're seeing hooch, and a periodic health check-in, so a slow patch is something you can actually spot and troubleshoot rather than just a vague feeling that things seem off lately.</p>

  <div class="callout printable-extras">
    <strong>Printable:</strong>
    <a href="/downloads/Sourdough_Starter_Maintenance_Log_v1.pdf" class="pdf-pill">Starter Log Template (PDF)</a>
  </div>

  <p>New to starters entirely? The site's Starter Guide (coming soon) covers creating one from scratch, maintaining it, and reading when it's actually ready to bake with.</p>

</PageLayout>
